### POST /v1/matchmaking/tickets — enqueue a player for matchmaking
###
### When to use: when a player starts searching for a match. Requires a valid
### Bearer token (run auth-service POST /v1/auth/login first — it captures
### `token`).
###
### How to use: run the requests below in order. The happy-path response
### captures `ticketId` for the GET ticket requests. Re-running the same
### `Idempotency-Key` returns the same ticket instead of duplicating it.
###
### Expected happy path: 201 with { "ticketId", "status": "SEARCHING", "skill", "searchRange", ... }.
### Error cases: invalid payload → 400; missing token → 401.

@apiBaseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Happy path — expect 201
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}/v1/matchmaking/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-key-1

{
  "gameMode": "5v5",
  "region": "NA",
  "maxLatencyMs": 80
}

> {% client.global.set("ticketId", response.body.ticketId); %}

### Idempotent replay — same Idempotency-Key returns the SAME ticketId
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}/v1/matchmaking/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-key-1

{
  "gameMode": "5v5",
  "region": "NA",
  "maxLatencyMs": 80
}

### Error case — missing fields → expect 400
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}/v1/matchmaking/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "gameMode": "5v5"
}

### Error case — no token → expect 401
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}/v1/matchmaking/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "gameMode": "5v5",
  "region": "NA",
  "maxLatencyMs": 80
}
